From 6570d09a6300e7f653f076a2fcd51fbf0596c4c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:17:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0150 -- event-dispatch and script-side cost
 attribution

Consolidates 0150, 0151, 0154, 0155, 0156, 0157, 0158, 0159, 0179, 0180 and
0181, across ac/event.cpp, ac/file.cpp, ac/global_game.cpp and ac/object.cpp.

Why. Blocking ticks of several seconds (AfterFadein at 7.53 s per dispatch on
hardware, 11-13% script_vm) sat behind one process_events_dispatch bracket
that was six different things. Each candidate is bracketed instead of argued:
- 0150/0151: per-event-type and per-room-event cost.
- 0154: the interaction run alone, by subtraction from the per-event total.
- 0155/0156/0157: the AfterFadein pre-amble. 0155 opened its scope too early
  and swallowed run_on_event; 0157 closes it where the logging ends. Only the
  corrected scope is in the tree, and that mis-scope is why "AfterFadein is
  our own logging" was retracted.
- 0158: SaveScreenShot, to separate the fixture's own overhead.
- 0159: nested-tick time inside the dispatch, to tell a screen that keeps
  animating from one that freezes.
- 0179: Object_SetView / Animate / SetVisible, the per-object scene-setup cost.
- 0180: the script_vm delta inside the dispatch, so it decomposes instead of
  leaving a residual.
- 0181: sc_OpenFile / WriteRawLine / Close, the script's own file I/O.

Timing only; no control flow changes. Needs dos_tick_nested_us from 0140.

Provenance of this export (2026-09-21): these edits sat uncommitted in the
vendor tree from patch 0123 onward, which is why every gate cell since said
build_dirty=1. They were made under one campaign-wide patch counter shared
with vendor/SDL, and each hunk carries its number in an in-source comment.
Intermediate states were never committed, so this patch is a hunk-level
partition of the final tree by concern, attributed by those comments -- not a
replay of the order the edits were made in, and its intermediate state was not
built on its own. The numbers named below are the ones found in its hunks.

